In particular it's good to know the history.  Google has a burp like
that every few months.  It's been happening every so often for
years at this point.  There's no notice that they are doing mantenance
it just spools posts for a while.  Often between 1 and 2 days.

When it comes down to it the design of UseNet assumes that
messages can take considerable time to propagate.  Sure, it's
wonderfull when a post makes it to all major servers on-line in
a couple of hours so same-day discussions can happen, but
that's never been an expectation on UseNet.  When posting
you should have the expectation that you'll get replies the next
day.  When posting through Google you should have the
expectation that posts will be queued as long as two days
before making it out.

